Description: Implements algorithms for terrestrial, mobile, and airborne lidar processing, tree detection, 
      segmentation, and attribute estimation (Donager et al., 2021) <doi:10.3390/rs13122297>, and hierarchical habitat
      patch delineation using 'PatchMorph' (Girvetz & Greco, 2007) <doi:10.1007/s10980-007-9104-8>. Tree detection
      combines point-cloud density, geometric metrics, and cylinder fitting to identify stems and estimate tree
      attributes. Segmentation methods include graph-based, allometric, geodesic, random-walker, and supervoxel 
      approaches for individual tree delineation from terrestrial and airborne lidar data. Additional tools support
      stem classification, bole segmentation, volume estimation, tree quality assessment, canopy structure analysis
      (LAI and PAD), and iterative model refinement. Built on 'lidR' (Roussel et al., 2020) <doi:10.1016/j.rse.2020.112061>.
